# Transcoded responsive photo variants (~17 MB). Production serves
# these from the public `<project>-assets` GCS bucket (uploaded by
# `cli assets upload`), so normal `COPY server server` image builds must not
# bundle local pulled photos. The deploy workflow's ephemeral KIND build
# verifies the real public origin, writes generated placeholders, and
# removes this ignore rule in its temporary checkout before building.
# The rest of `server/public` (Bootstrap, brand SVGs) still ships.
server/public/img/
# Licensed GORP WOFF2 files are served from the deployment asset origin; the
# real bytes are never baked into an application image. Handled exactly like
# the photos above: the ephemeral KIND build stubs them and drops this rule so
# the local `/public` mount serves the same keys the public origin does.
server/public/fonts/gorp-serif/*.woff2
